      "mergeID": "626a0caf3235d352a364c79c",
      "mergedPostDetails": "When testing the new bio feature  in-game, I came across a situation where the automatic censorship filtering erroneously \"fixes\" a bio. \n\nThis is reproducible using these steps:\n\n1) Write a bio\n2) Somewhere in the bio, add the word \"shit\".\n3) You will see that it gets converted to \"poop\".\n4) Try Changing \"poop\" to \"sh1t\" (Use a '1' instead of an i).\n5) The bio now has lost all of its formatting, capitalization, and spacing.\n\nSee images below for a before and after. This likely isn't a client issue but rather server-side, specifically the censorship script breaking when trying to parse \"workaround-swears\". I noticed that the '4' in \"4-year veteren\" got turned into an 'a', leading me to believe the issue lies in the string sanitization.",
      "mergedPostTitle": "[1101] Bio Censor Filter Removes Spaces, Capitalization, and Formatting when changing Bio In-game",
      "pinned": false,
      "postID": "602acad5e5e235547b02ac19",
      "private": false,
      "spam": false,
      "synthetic": true,
      "value": ""
    },
