      "mergeID": "626a0fc6f5b4701a28165ea3",
      "mergedPostDetails": "I tried to upload an avatar of a character named \"Kanami Mashita\" and it filtered it to \"Kanami Mapoopa.\" While profanity filters are fine for things like English-language text chat, they should never be used for name fields—any attempt to algorithmically determine what is or is not a name will automatically be racist in its attempt to filter names from other languages by the specific rules of one arbitrary language (English). I suggest that this filter be removed entirely.",
      "mergedPostTitle": "Avatar name filter overzealously matches real names",
      "pinned": false,
      "postID": "602acad5e5e235547b02ac19",
      "private": false,
      "spam": false,
